    "definitions": {
      "short": "a plan , usually evil ( machination ), sometimes good ( sagacity )",
      "usage": "(wicked) device, discretion, intent, witty invention, lewdness, mischievous (device), thought, wickedly.",
      "full": "H4209. mezimmah מְזִמָּה noun feminine purpose, discretion, device (Jeremiah and Wisdom Literature), מְזִמָּה Job 42:2 5 t.; הַמְּזִמָּ֫תָה Jer 11:15 **altogether תָעָתֵךְ מֵעָלַיִח יִעֲבִרוּ קֹדֶשׁ וּבְשַׂר ַהנְדָרִים מְזִמֹּת עָֽשְׂתָה (but read for ׳המ רַבִּים with ַהנְדָרִים הַמְּזִמֹּת ᵐ5 ); מְזִמָּתוֺ 51:11 ; plural absolute מְזִמּוֺת Psa 37:7 7 t.; construct id. Jer 23:20 ; 30:24 ; suffix מְזִמּוֺתָיו Psa 10:4 ; &#8212; 1 of ׳י 's purposes Job 42:2 ; chiefly in punishment (compare זִמָּה זָמַם, ) Jer 23:20 ; 30:24 ; 51:11 (|| זמם 51:12 ). 2 power of devising, discretion Prov 1:4 (|| דַּעַת ), 2:11 (|| תְּבוּנָה ), 3:21 (|| תֻּשִׁיָּה ), 5:2 (|| דַּעַת ); מְזִמּוֺת דַּעַת 8:12 . 3. a. evil thoughts of men Psa 10:4 , evil devices of men Job 21:27 (|| מחשׁבות ), Psa 10:2 ; 21:12 (both with חָשַׁב ). b. wickedness in act Jer 11:15 ; Psa 37:7 (both with עָשָׂה ), 139:20 לִמְזִמָּה = wickedly ; — note phrases: אישׁ מְזִמּוֺת a man of (evil) devices (or practices ) Prov 12:2 (opposed to טוֺכ ) 14:17 ; בַּעַלמְֿזִמּוֺת 24:8 (|| לְהָרֵעַ מְחַשֵּׁב ; see בַּעַל ).",
